NAME
    mkdir - create a directory

SYNOPSIS
    mkdir path

DESCRIPTION
    Creates a new, empty subdirectory at the given path. Prints "DIR
    CREATED" on success.

    mkdir is an OS built-in command (unlike del/help, which moved to /bin):
    it is a filesystem BOOTSTRAP primitive -- you need it to create /bin on
    a freshly-formatted card before any /bin program can exist, and format
    wipes /bin, so it cannot depend on a /bin binary. (It shares the work
    with the SYS_MKDIR syscall that /bin programs like cp use.)

EXAMPLES
    mkdir /src
    mkdir sub

SEE ALSO
    rmdir, cd, dir
